+# Password Hashing
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use argon2id as the password hashing algorithm for the authentication layer. It was chosen because it is a memory-hard algorithm that resists GPU-accelerated brute-force attacks, which the project prioritizes for long-term password security. No further parameters (such as memory cost, iteration count, or parallelism) are recorded, so none are specified here.
